/*
====================================================
LIVE DATA – THEORY & CONCEPTS (WITH EXPLANATION)
====================================================

WHAT IS LiveData?
-----------------
LiveData is a lifecycle-aware observable data holder.
It means:
- It holds data
- It can be observed
- It automatically updates the UI when data changes
- It respects the lifecycle of UI components


WHY NOT USE A NORMAL VARIABLE?
------------------------------

Example of normal variable:

    var count = 0

Problems with normal variable:
1) UI is NOT notified when value changes
2) Manual UI update is required
3) Not lifecycle-aware
4) Can cause bugs during configuration changes
5) Not suitable for reactive UI (Jetpack Compose)

Normal variable flow (BAD):
Button Click → count++ → UI DOES NOT KNOW ABOUT CHANGE


WHY LiveData IS BETTER
---------------------

LiveData solves the above problems.

Key advantages:

1) OBSERVABLE
   LiveData allows UI to observe data changes.

   Example:
       counter.observe(...)

   Whenever value changes, observers are notified automatically.

2) LIFECYCLE-AWARE
   LiveData updates UI only when:
   - Activity / Composable is active
   - Prevents memory leaks
   - Stops updates when UI is destroyed

3) AUTOMATIC UI UPDATE (COMPOSE)
   Using observeAsState():

       val count by liveData.observeAsState(0)

   When LiveData value changes:
   - Compose recomposes automatically
   - No manual UI refresh needed

4) SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH
   Data is stored in one place (LiveData)
   UI only reads data
   Business logic updates data

   This avoids:
   - Inconsistent UI
   - Multiple sources updating same value


DATA FLOW USING LiveData
------------------------

Button Click
    ↓
LiveData value changes
    ↓
Observers are notified
    ↓
Compose recomposes UI automatically


WHY LiveData IS IMPORTANT IN ANDROID
------------------------------------

- Android UI has lifecycle (created, started, destroyed)
- LiveData understands lifecycle
- Normal variables do NOT

This makes LiveData safe, reliable, and scalable.


INTERVIEW-READY DEFINITIONS
---------------------------

"LiveData is a lifecycle-aware observable data holder class
that updates the UI automatically when data changes."

"LiveData is preferred over normal variables because it
supports observation, lifecycle awareness, and automatic UI updates."


WHEN TO USE LiveData
-------------------

- When UI depends on changing data
- When multiple UI components observe same data
- When lifecycle safety is required
- When building reactive UI (Compose / XML)


SUMMARY
-------

Normal Variable:
- Holds data only
- No observation
- No lifecycle awareness

LiveData:
- Holds data
- Observable
- Lifecycle-aware
- Automatic UI updates
- Recommended for Android UI

====================================================
END OF THEORY
====================================================
*/
